; provenance=true is intentionally OFF for local publishes.
;
; npm can only generate a provenance attestation from a supported CI provider
; (GitHub Actions / GitLab CI) with an OIDC token — from a laptop it fails hard
; with "Automatic provenance generation not supported for provider: null" and
; the publish never happens.
;
; Turn it back on the moment publishing moves into CI: provenance is a real
; supply-chain signal (it ties the tarball to the commit and workflow that
; built it), and this package asks people to run it against their own
; transcripts, so that signal is worth having.
